  "provenance": {
    "pattern": "afro house: the four under interlocking hand drums on a twelve-against-four feel, a sixteenth shaker, a soft clap on two and four, an open hat on the offbeat and a sparse, syncopated bass",
    "knowledge": "public knowledge of the genre: the pattern as drummers, producers and tutorials commonly write it; no recording was sampled, transcribed from audio or mined",
    "note": "Two bars. The hand drums play the three-against-two of the clave family (a son-clave-shaped line in the first bar, its answer in the second) with fills; a sixteenth shaker under them; the clap soft on two and four; an open hat on each and. The bass leaves the one and lands on the a of one and the and of three. Swing 0.56 on the percussion."
  }
